meta {
  name: Run tape (whole script)
  type: http
  seq: 42
}

get {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/sim/tape?deviceId={{deviceId}}
  body: none
  auth: none
}

docs {
  The mock feed as a tape, so the device plays the race from RAM instead of
  refetching a wall-clock window every ~30s (that is what skipped the first
  130s of race 182, and what left 13s holes in tracks). text/plain:

  #runId,sessionId,gunSec,durationSec,totalFixes,serverEpoch
  epoch,lat,lon,speed,course      (one line per 1Hz fix, epoch = seconds)

  sessionId is what the device gates on: a journey may not sail until the
  race screen is up AND the engine holds that same session, because the
  engine is what scores it (a journey that starts first has wasted its
  front — race 182).

  No live run? The same tape carries the server-driven WALK instead
  (runId "wander", 30 fixes) — one URL and one reader for the device.
  ?from= / ?n= page a journey longer than the device's tape. 404 only when
  there is no run AND nothing at all to seed a walk from.
}
